{
  "requirement": "Usage MUST record mandatory input counts and sizes by evidence kind, in UTF-8\nbytes and lines, and the same information for additional inputs requested through\n`habeas` or `ripgrep`. A requirements input MUST also record its number of matched declarations.\nUsage MUST distinguish unique inputs from repeated reads, successful from\nfailed reads, and prepared inputs from those actually sent to the model.\nFile-discovery calls MUST count as tool calls without recording directory\nlistings as evidence or source inputs.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "## Verdict\nThe `usage_inputs` implementation is complete and correctly marked, and the tests cover its main behaviors. There is one interpretive weak point, described at the end.\n\n## Implementation\n\n**Counts and sizes by evidence kind (`src/authoring/usage.rs`, `UsageLog::prepared`, `InputUsage`)**\n- Every prepared input becomes an `InputUsage` entry with `origin`, `kind`, `bytes`, `lines`, `components`, `unique`, `submitted_in_request` and `sent_in_request`.\n- `kind` is `outline`, `requirements` or `definition`.\n- `bytes` is the sum of `str::len` over the text lines plus the joined newlines, so it counts UTF-8 bytes.\n- `lines` is `text.len()`.\n- `configured_record` in `src/authoring/mod.rs` calls `usage.prepared(\"mandatory\", sources.mandatory_inputs())`.\n- `assess` calls `usage.prepared(<tool name>, &delivery.inputs)` for each successful tool call. Additional inputs from `habeas` and `ripgrep` are therefore recorded with their own origin and the same metrics. The deliveries include `habeas` and `ripgrep` terminology definitions.\n\n**Matched declarations for a requirements input**\n- `components` is `matches.len()` for inputs that have `matches`, and 1 otherwise.\n\n**Unique versus repeated reads**\n- `unique` is set from `self.seen.insert(input.to_string())`, so a repeated delivery is recorded as a repeat rather than dropped.\n\n**Successful versus failed reads**\n- `UsageLog::tool(name, failed)` increments `tool_calls` and, on failure, `tool_failures`, per tool.\n- `assess` calls it with `failed = true` on dispatch errors and `false` on success.\n- Failed reads produce no input entries.\n- Unknown tool names are bucketed as `unknown`, so model-supplied text never reaches the log.\n\n**Prepared versus actually sent**\n- `begin_request` stamps `submitted_in_request` on every input that has none yet.\n- `end_request` stamps `sent_in_request` only when the provider returned usage, meaning the request completed. Failed or retried requests leave it unset.\n- Inputs that were prepared but never sent keep `sent_in_request` null. This happens, for example, when a permission denial aborts the run.\n\n**File discovery**\n- `list_files` returns `inputs: Vec::new()` in `src/authoring/tools.rs`.\n- `assess` still calls `usage.tool(\"list_files\", false)`, so the call counts as a tool call. `prepared` receives an empty slice, so nothing is recorded as an input.\n\n**Marking**\n- `prepared`, `begin_request`, `end_request`, `tool`, `skipped_tool`, `InputUsage`, `configured_record` and `assess` carry `{impl}` references.\n- I found no unmarked behavior that implements part of this requirement. `tool_name` is marked for `usage_requests` and `usage_storage` but not `usage_inputs`. That is a trivial omission.\n- I found no unspecified behavior in the `usage_inputs` implementation beyond the requirement's scope.\n\n## Tests\n\n**`usage.rs::input_metadata_counts_components_and_reads_without_persisting_source`**\n- Checks `kind`, UTF-8 byte count (including the multibyte \"λ\"), `lines`, `components` of 2 for a requirements input, `unique` true then false for a repeat, and `origin`.\n- Checks the full lifecycle: prepared (both request fields null), then submitted, then sent.\n- Checks that no source text, file name, selector or match name is persisted.\n\n**`usage.rs::failed_submission_can_be_confirmed_on_a_later_attempt`**\n- A failed request leaves `sent_in_request` null.\n- A retry sets `sent_in_request` to the retry index, while `submitted_in_request` stays at the first attempt.\n\n**`usage.rs::tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text`**\n- `list_files` and `outline` are counted as tool calls with an empty `inputs` array.\n- Failures and skips are distinguished.\n\n**`mod.rs::throttled_requests_retry_unchanged_and_record_every_attempt`**\n- Covers the eight-failure retry case: every input has `submitted_in_request` 0 and `sent_in_request` 8.\n\n**`tests/authoring_cli.rs::ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free`**\n- An end-to-end run covering `list_files`, `ripgrep`, a repeated `habeas` read and a failed `habeas` read of `absent.txt`.\n- Asserts `tool_calls.habeas` 3 and `tool_failures.habeas` 1.\n- Asserts a repeated `habeas` input with `unique == false` and `sent_in_request == 1`.\n- Asserts a mandatory definition input with `bytes > 0`.\n- Asserts that no secrets appear in the usage record.\n\n**`tools.rs` tests**\n- Assert that `list_files`, `outline` and `references` return empty `inputs`.\n\n## Weak point\nCounts \"by evidence kind\" are recorded as per-input entries that carry `kind`, not as pre-aggregated per-kind totals. Per-kind counts and sizes are directly derivable from the stored data. I read this as satisfying the requirement and did not treat it as a gap.\n\nThere are no FIXME markers or acknowledged gaps.",
  "references": "d98ad053bd25f19d40a49705d2abdee1c2038a443fcedafbf2030da92906d1cc",
